Limits of this attribution
--------------------------

ECDICT is released under the MIT License by its author, and this project
relies on that grant. However, ECDICT is itself a compilation assembled over
many years. Per its own README, the corpus grew from community contributions,
the open-source cdict-1.0-1.rpm dictionary, the English-Chinese portion of the
open-source 屌丝字典 (https://github.com/fxsjy/diaosi), and proofreading passes
against the BNC and COCA frequency lists.

Neither this project nor its author can verify the provenance of individual
entries within that 768,000-row corpus, and no such claim is made here. What
can be stated is narrower and checkable:

  * ECDICT is distributed by its author under the MIT License.
  * This repository contains no ECDICT data. build_dict.py fetches it from a
    pinned upstream commit and verifies its SHA-256 on the user's own machine.
  * Consequently this project redistributes no dictionary content, and any
    question about the upstream corpus should be directed at ECDICT itself:
    https://github.com/skywind3000/ECDICT

If you intend to deploy this in a commercial or institutional setting where
data provenance matters, evaluate the upstream project on its own terms rather
than relying on this notice.


